ks","titel":"","waarde":{"velden":[{"veld":"item-categorie","titel":"Category","waarde":"Freshman course Bachelor"},{"veld":"item-voertaal","titel":"Instruction language","waarde":"English"}]}},{"veld":"regio-rechts","titel":"","waarde":{"velden":[{"veld":"item-opmerking","titel":"Remark","waarde":"Caution: this information is subject to change"}]}}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-inhoud","titel":"Aims and content","weergave":"UIT","velden":[{"veld":"item-inhoud-1","titel":"Aims","waarde":"<html lang=\"null\"><head><title></title><style type=\"text/css\">body { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial } table { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial }</style></head><body><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:0cm;line-height:16.0pt;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;' data-pasted=\"true\"><u><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>Knowledge</span></u><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>: after following this course the student will be able to:</span></p><div style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;'><ol style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;list-style-type: decimal;margin-left: 8px;\"><li style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family: initial;\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;font-size:16px;'>Explain recent theories and issues concerning critical and digital heritage, including the emergence and development of concepts of heritage in the nineteenth and twentieth century and understand their relevance today.&nbsp;</span></li><li style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family: initial;\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;font-size:16px;'>Explain recent theories and issues concerning cultural memory and dealing with the past.&nbsp;</span></li><li style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family: initial;\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;font-size:16px;'>Apply knowledge from critical heritage studies and cultural memory studies in the analysis of various case studies: objects, monuments, institutions, rituals, digital platforms, with a focus on identity, power, agency, and the affordances of the digital realm.&nbsp;</span></li></ol></div><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:0cm;line-height:16.0pt;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;'><u><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>Skills</span></u><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>: after following this course the student will be able to:</span></p><div style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;'><ol start=\"4\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;list-style-type: decimal;margin-left: 8px;\"><li style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family: initial;\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;font-size:16px;'>Apply academic writing principles to write an academic paper for <em>Diggit Magazine</em> in which students demonstrate their understanding of the concepts and issues in critical heritage studies and / or cultural memory studies.&nbsp;</span></li></ol></div><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:0cm;line-height:16.0pt;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;'><u><span style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;\"></span></u><u><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>Character building</span></u><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>:&nbsp;</span></p><div style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;'><ol start=\"5\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;list-style-type: decimal;margin-left: 8px;\"><li style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:14px;font-family: initial;\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;font-size:16px;'>In this course students are trained as intellectually independent thinkers. They have to collect and evaluate information from reliable sources for the writing assignments about heritage practices and to show a nuanced understanding of the (contested) topics they write about.</span></li></ol></div></body></html>"},{"veld":"item-inhoud-2","titel":"Content","waarde":"<html lang=\"null\"><head><title></title><style type=\"text/css\">body { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial } table { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial }</style></head><body><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:0cm;line-height:16.0pt;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;' data-pasted=\"true\"><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>Heritage is a dynamic concept with various manifestations. Discussions of heritage that circulate today are never straightforward and often concern questions of power and perspective. Heritage can be institutionalized, or non-institutionalized. It can be celebrated or contested. As culture studies academics, it is important for us to cast a critical eye on these issues. This course will invite you to ask what the most pressing and critical questions are concerning (digital) heritage today. These questions might include: How do communities deal with the past? Who makes decisions on what should be remembered, and what should not? What role do the internet and digital technologies play in the safeguarding of heritage, and how might this change in the future? How should western galleries respond to the pressure of repatriating objects acquired from formerly colonized places? How might public debates about history and heritage affect our notions of heritage in the future?&nbsp;</span></p><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:0cm;line-height:16.0pt;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;text-indent:36.0pt;'><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>These discussions emerge from contexts of globalization and decolonization, and they are particularly important in our present digital age. In this course we will also explore the thematization of heritage in art, and the place of heritage in activism. This course will draw together insights from digital and public humanities, critical heritage studies, ritual studies, memory studies, and museum studies.&nbsp;</span></p><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:0cm;line-height:16.0pt;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;'><br /></p><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:0cm;line-height:16.0pt;font-size:14px;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif;'><span style='font-size:16px;font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif;'>Part of this course is training in academic writing and academic reading. The <u>writing skills</u> will be trained by two formative assignments as preparation for the final <em>Diggit</em> essay. Students will be trained in techniques of <u>academic reading</u> by taking the LibGuide &lsquo;Academic Reading&rsquo; and applying these techniques to new academic texts, both with and without the support of AI-tools as teaching assistants.&nbsp;</span></p></body></html>"}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-vrije-velden","titel":"Additional information","weergave":"UIT","velden":[{"veld":"item-vrij-veld-23","titel":"Contact person","gegevenstype":"TEKST","waarde":"<a href=\"https://www.tilburguniversity.edu/nl/medewerkers/m-j-m-hoondert\" target=\"_blank\">dr. M.J.M. Hoondert</a>"}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-toetsen","titel":"Tests","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-toetsen","titel":"Tests","waarde":[{"omschrijving":"Diggit Paper (70%)","samengestelde-toets":"","is_onderliggend_toets":"N","is_bovenliggende_toets":"N","velden":[{"veld":"item-toets-weging","titel":"Test weight","waarde":"70"},{"veld":"item-toets-resultaatschaal","titel":"Grading scale","waarde":"ten points, two decimal places"}]},{"omschrijving":"Mini Essay (30%)","samengestelde-toets":"","is_onderliggend_toets":"N","is_bovenliggende_toets":"N","velden":[{"veld":"item-toets-weging","titel":"Test weight","waarde":"30"},{"veld":"item-toets-resultaatschaal","titel":"Grading scale","waarde":"ten points, two decimal places"}]}]}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-inschrijven","titel":"Course enrolment","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-inschrijfperiodes","titel":"Enrolment periods","waarde":[{"omschrijving":"Semester 1","id_cursus_inschrijving":1143776,"velden":[]}]}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-docenten","titel":"Lecturers","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-docenten","titel":"Lecturers","waarde":[{"omschrijving":"Lecturer","velden":[{"docent":"dr. M.J.M. Hoondert","url_medewerker":"","velden":[]}]}]}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-materialen","titel":"Materials","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-materialen","titel":"","waarde":[{"omschrijving":"Required material","velden":[{"materiaal":"To be announced","velden":[{"veld":"item-materiaal-omschrijving","titel":"","waarde":"Literature will be shared through Canvas."}]}]}]}]}],"hasMore":false,"limit":0,"offset":0,"count":10}